/*
 * conf/test.config — minimal `test` profile placeholder.
 *
 * STATUS: stub only. The full "synthetic-data CI/smoke-test profile" described
 * in this repo's CLAUDE.md roadmap ("conf/test.config -- minimal test profile
 * with synthetic data for CI/smoke testing") has not been built yet -- no
 * synthetic samplesheet/references are bundled here. This file exists only so
 * that `nextflow.config`'s `profiles { test { includeConfig 'conf/test.config' } }`
 * block resolves to a real file.
 *
 * Why this matters even if you never use `-profile test`: Nextflow >= ~25.x
 * eagerly validates every `includeConfig` path across ALL profile blocks at
 * config-parse time, not just the profile actually selected on the command
 * line. Before this stub existed, `nextflow run main.nf -profile standard`
 * (or `-profile slurm`) failed outright with
 * "Invalid include source: conf/test.config" even though the `test` profile
 * was never requested -- discovered 2026-07-15 while smoke-testing the
 * v2.0.0 host-quant arm locally with Nextflow 26.04.6 (self-installed via
 * get.nextflow.io). Juno's pinned Nextflow build
 * (/groups/tprice/pipelines/bin/nextflow) may be an older version that
 * doesn't eagerly validate unselected profiles, so this may not have
 * manifested there yet -- but it will on any future Nextflow upgrade, on
 * Juno or elsewhere, so it's fixed here rather than left latent.
 *
 * To build out the real synthetic-data test profile later: point
 * params.samplesheet at a small synthetic paired-end FASTQ samplesheet,
 * and params.star_index / kraken2_db at small reference builds (see
 * docs/tooling_progress_plan.md and the toy chr21 STAR index recipe used for
 * the v2.0.0 host-quant-arm smoke test for a working pattern).
 */

process.executor = 'local'
